1
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:35,030
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,259 --> 00:01:37,740
[Episode 6]

3
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,150
Zheng.

4
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:42,000
You served

5
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,729
in the military before, right?

6
00:01:44,030 --> 00:01:44,590
Yes.

7
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,310
I heard Court Pres. Zhang

8
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:49,440
also came over from the military
to take up his post here.

9
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:52,920
I don't really understand

10
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,320
the professional stuff.

11
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:55,400
But why do I feel

12
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,759
that Court Pres. Ding

13
00:01:57,759 --> 00:01:58,680
drags his feet too much

14
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,210
when handing down rulings.

15
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:04,250
Court Pres. Ding is just cautious.

16
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:05,640
He always reminds us

17
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:06,710
that there are no small matters in law,

18
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,840
so nothing can be treated carelessly.

19
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,000
We military men

20
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:12,770
do things decisively.

21
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,840
Get the facts straight,
make a firm decision,

22
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:18,190
and hand down the ruling
according to the law.

23
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:19,120
But look at this.

24
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:22,079
Tried but not sentenced.
Sentenced but not executed.

25
00:02:22,079 --> 00:02:23,030
After months of dragging on,

26
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:25,230
the public's patience is wearing thin.

27
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:28,800
Even if they do execute the criminal
in the end,

28
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,400
the impact

29
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:30,840
will be long gone.

30
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:31,840
Don't you agree?

31
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:32,770
I agree.

32
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,600
Which case are you referring to?

33
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:46,840
What the defense laywer said

34
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,240
is not unreasonable.

35
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:49,840
These two

36
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,579
maintained this relationship

37
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,740
for nearly 4 years.

38
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,360
During that time, the woman

39
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,290
even wrote love letters to the man.

40
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,120
It's not

41
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,000
entirely out of the question

42
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,200
that it was adultery.

43
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,460
Court Pres. Zhang.

44
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:08,310
What's your opinion

45
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,000
on this case?

46
00:03:11,770 --> 00:03:12,840
This case...

47
00:03:13,190 --> 00:03:14,560
You guys talk.

48
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:15,870
I don't know the law,

49
00:03:15,870 --> 00:03:17,030
and I'm new here.

50
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,100
My opinion carries no weight.

51
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:20,680
Court Pres. Zhang,

52
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,960
you're being way too modest.

53
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,870
You were sent here by the higher-ups

54
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,470
to oversee our work.

55
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:26,730
So your opinion

56
00:03:26,910 --> 00:03:27,870
matters a lot.

57
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:30,520
Okay.

58
00:03:31,150 --> 00:03:32,110
Then I'll just speak my mind

59
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:33,310
for everyone's consideration,

60
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:33,750
okay?

61
00:03:35,430 --> 00:03:37,430
My opinion is actually very simple.

62
00:03:37,470 --> 00:03:38,120
Two words.

63
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:40,440
Execute him.

64
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,400
Court Pres. Ding.

65
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,470
If this case

66
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,960
doesn't end with an immediate execution,

67
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:58,780
do you think

68
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:00,470
the public

69
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:02,030
will accept that?

70
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,769
The defendant, Qiao Zhiliang,

71
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,560
using his special status

72
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:21,120
and

73
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:23,630
family connections,

74
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:25,350
employed coercive means

75
00:04:25,710 --> 00:04:27,780
to forcibly engage

76
00:04:27,950 --> 00:04:29,680
in sexual relations with the victim.

77
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,480
His actions

78
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,159
have constituted the crime of rape.

79
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:36,070
The circumstances of the crime
are egregious,

80
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:38,360
causing severe harm

81
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,159
to the victim and her family.

82
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:43,950
The social impact is extremely damaging.

83
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:46,280
It is indeed
a crime of the utmost severity

84
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:49,159
and must be punished according to the law.

85
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:54,240
In accordance with Article 139

86
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:57,430
of the Criminal Law
of the People's Republic of China,

87
00:04:57,680 --> 00:05:01,120
the defendant, Qiao Zhiliang,
is hereby sentenced to death

88
00:05:02,630 --> 00:05:05,030
and deprived of political rights for life.

89
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:16,780
Defendant,

90
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,630
you have three days to appeal.

91
00:05:20,630 --> 00:05:22,680
Do you wish to file an appeal?

92
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:42,310
Take the defendant away.

93
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:44,190
Court is adjourned.

94
00:06:14,190 --> 00:06:15,520
We need to do something.

95
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:17,310
Don't stir up more trouble.

96
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:19,640
Court Pres. Ding has got enough problems.

97
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,750
They said
some Vice Court Pres. Zhang came,

98
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,430
but he's really just an overseer.

99
00:06:23,430 --> 00:06:24,800
He keeps breathing down Ding's neck.

100
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,800
You're actually feeling sorry for Ding?

101
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,750
Cadres indeed always
stick up for one another.

102
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,720
That old Ding Zhongxiang
clearly handed down a ridiculous verdict!

103
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:31,430
Although it was rape,

104
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:32,800
it was hardly a capital offense.

105
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,200
You never shut up, do you?

106
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,630
Article 43 of the criminal law states

107
00:06:41,630 --> 00:06:42,830
that the death penalty shall only apply

108
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:44,760
to criminals
whose crimes are extremely heinous.

109
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:46,050
For those criminals

110
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:47,040
who deserve the death penalty,

111
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,870
if immediate execution is not necessary,

112
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:51,400
they may be given
a suspended death sentence.

113
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:52,630
In this case,

114
00:06:52,950 --> 00:06:54,550
even if it's a death penalty,

115
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:57,290
there's no need
for immediate execution, right?

116
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,970
Let's go find Court Pres. Ding.

117
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:05,270
I, uh...

118
00:07:05,710 --> 00:07:06,770
I just saw the Court Pres. Ding

119
00:07:06,770 --> 00:07:07,530
in his office.

120
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:09,460
If we go now, we can still catch him.

121
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:10,650
Let's go!

122
00:07:11,710 --> 00:07:13,440
Let's corner Ding Zhongxiang.

123
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:14,250
Let's go.

124
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,100
Yu Gaoyuan, are you coming or not?

125
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:20,460
Of course.

126
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,020
Why wouldn't I?

127
00:07:31,870 --> 00:07:33,000
All of you together?

128
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:34,450
Sit down.

129
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:35,650
Please sit down.

130
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:37,159
Sit down.

131
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:41,630
Have you eaten?

132
00:07:41,630 --> 00:07:42,960
I just finished eating.

133
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,040
Court Pres. Ding,

134
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,830
we think
the verdict in Qiao Zhiliang's case

135
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:49,930
is problematic.

136
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:52,040
You again.

137
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:53,750
You little rebel.

138
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,120
Court Pres. Ding.

139
00:07:56,530 --> 00:07:57,480
We've all reviewed

140
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,740
Qiao Zhiliang's case.

141
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:59,600
If...

142
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,450
it's considered adultery,

143
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:04,360
it might not even warrant
criminal punishment.

144
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,870
If it's considered rape,

145
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,750
it still shouldn't warrant
the death penalty.

146
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:10,120
Isn't the death penalty

147
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:12,000
a bit much here?

148
00:08:16,190 --> 00:08:17,270
What do you think

149
00:08:19,950 --> 00:08:21,210
the public's reaction

150
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:22,360
would be

151
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:24,910
if we didn't sentence him

152
00:08:25,310 --> 00:08:26,190
to death?

153
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:31,580
Young lady,

154
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:32,809
you tell me.

155
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,840
There would be a lot of opposition.

156
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,390
They might even storm the court.

157
00:08:39,390 --> 00:08:40,600
Future trials

158
00:08:40,659 --> 00:08:42,260
might lose all credibility.

159
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,860
That's way too honest.

160
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,020
Look at you.

161
00:08:47,910 --> 00:08:50,170
College students really are different.

162
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:51,760
That analytical ability

163
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:53,180
is something else.

164
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,440
Court Pres. Ding,

165
00:08:54,910 --> 00:08:56,450
the law should be rational,

166
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,270
objective,

167
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,530
and principled.

168
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,750
Our rulings

169
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:01,870
shouldn't be swayed

170
00:09:01,870 --> 00:09:03,070
by public sentiment.

171
00:09:05,030 --> 00:09:06,910
You all make valid points.

172
00:09:08,170 --> 00:09:09,560
But today I am

173
00:09:10,870 --> 00:09:12,360
so exhausted.

174
00:09:13,630 --> 00:09:15,360
From this morning till now,

175
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,790
I haven't had a single bite.

176
00:09:18,910 --> 00:09:19,600
How about

177
00:09:20,630 --> 00:09:21,830
you let me off the hook

178
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:23,870
for now?

179
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:26,240
Ding!

180
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:29,570
Look at this crowd.

181
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:30,220
Shang.

182
00:09:30,390 --> 00:09:31,360
Come on over.

183
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,110
Have a seat.

184
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:32,880
Come on.

185
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:34,030
There are no strangers here.

186
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:34,690
Have a seat.

187
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,640
Don't stand on ceremony with me.

188
00:09:39,030 --> 00:09:40,080
Why are you all standing?

189
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:40,860
Sit down. Sit down.

190
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:41,390
Sit down.

191
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:43,480
Sit down. Come on.

192
00:09:45,150 --> 00:09:45,630
Ding.

193
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:46,970
Since I'm here,

194
00:09:46,970 --> 00:09:48,500
I'll keep this short today.

195
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:50,630
Out of the three death sentences here,

196
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:52,430
two have already been approved.

197
00:09:52,670 --> 00:09:55,270
Only Qiao Zhiliang's case
has yet to be approved.

198
00:09:55,270 --> 00:09:56,030
For God's sake,

199
00:09:56,030 --> 00:09:58,200
hurry up and get him to file an appeal.

200
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:05,480
But he refuses to appeal.

201
00:10:05,870 --> 00:10:07,750
If he doesn't appeal,

202
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:09,480
I have to sit around here

203
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,750
and wait 3 more days.

204
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:14,010
Then just wait 3 more days.

205
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:15,720
Shang.

206
00:10:16,030 --> 00:10:17,560
In our Intermediate Court,

207
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:18,530
how many appeals

208
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,600
have succeeded

209
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,960
and resulted in reversed judgments
this year?

210
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,820
I'll be straight with you.

211
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:29,600
Zero.

212
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:30,930
There you go.

213
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:32,630
Don't you think

214
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,870
our current procedure

215
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,670
is a bit too hasty?

216
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:38,680
When it's hasty,

217
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:40,690
mistakes are bound to happen.

218
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,440
It's about a person's life.

219
00:10:45,750 --> 00:10:47,550
You just need to wait 3 more days.

220
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:48,790
Is that

221
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:50,680
asking too much?

222
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:51,900
Alright, alright.

223
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,600
I'll wait. I'll wait, okay?

224
00:10:58,150 --> 00:10:58,600
Ding,

225
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:00,670
these are

226
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:03,390
the elite college students
you talked about?

227
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:04,390
Just look at them.

228
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:05,360
Every one of them

229
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,690
has got a silver tongue.

230
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:08,450
They're not to be messed with.

231
00:11:13,510 --> 00:11:15,000
The appeal deadline

232
00:11:15,030 --> 00:11:16,430
used to be within 10 days.

233
00:11:16,790 --> 00:11:18,390
Now it's been shortened to 3.

234
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,720
If an appeal is filed right away,

235
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,240
it gets rejected immediately.

236
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:24,360
Death penalty cases are somewhat special.

237
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:27,420
Is this driven
by the demands of the current situation?

238
00:11:27,870 --> 00:11:28,240
Yes.

239
00:11:29,150 --> 00:11:29,750
Dismissal

240
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:32,090
has almost become the default option.

241
00:11:32,290 --> 00:11:33,170
This leads

242
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,960
to the result you mentioned.

243
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:35,720
Appealing

244
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:37,920
actually makes them die faster.

245
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,960
Then why are you
still urging Qiao Zhiliang to appeal?

246
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,200
I want to keep trying.

247
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:45,270
I think

248
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:48,070
there is still a glimmer of hope for him.

249
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,500
Are you doing this

250
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:51,590
for your own unwillingness to let go

251
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:52,360
or

252
00:11:53,030 --> 00:11:53,910
for the good of your client?

253
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:55,510
Can you tell the difference?

254
00:11:58,030 --> 00:12:00,030
Qiao Zhiliang's case is different.

255
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:02,720
I want to see it through to the end.

256
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:03,240
Even if there's only

257
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,840
a one-in-a-million chance,

258
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,500
I don't want to give up.

259
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:33,080
Take a seat.

260
00:12:45,150 --> 00:12:46,080
I came here today

261
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,450
to ask you one last time.

262
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,970
Do you still want to appeal?

263
00:12:58,030 --> 00:12:59,240
If you appeal,

264
00:12:59,510 --> 00:13:01,080
I can't guarantee the outcome,

265
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:01,840
but I will definitely

266
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:02,720
try my best.

267
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:12,700
Qiao Zhiliang,

268
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:15,740
your wife hates you very much,

269
00:13:16,790 --> 00:13:18,920
but she doesn't want you to die either.

270
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:21,420
She's also doing her best to save you.

271
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,080
For her

272
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,540
and for your two children,

273
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:25,390
you can't

274
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:26,650
just give up like this.

275
00:13:37,770 --> 00:13:39,830
Death penalty cases can be appealed.

276
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:43,440
Please continue to have me
as your lawyer, okay?

277
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,390
During the second trial,

278
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:46,920
I will definitely
do everything I can for you.

279
00:13:54,110 --> 00:13:55,220
Qiao Zhiliang!

280
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,120
Even I haven't given up on you!

281
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:57,630
Why are you

282
00:13:57,630 --> 00:13:59,000
giving up on yourself?

283
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:01,910
Mr. Li.

284
00:14:04,390 --> 00:14:05,990
Thank you for your hard work.

285
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,280
We'll meet again if fate allows.

286
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,790
Li Xiang was just normally

287
00:15:09,790 --> 00:15:10,480
performing his duties

288
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,840
as a defense lawyer.

289
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:13,170
And for that,

290
00:15:13,550 --> 00:15:14,810
you want to arrest him?

291
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:17,240
That's not going to look good.

292
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:20,850
Wait a minute.

293
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:37,170
Go ahead.

294
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:42,910
Have some water.

295
00:15:42,910 --> 00:15:43,360
Don't bother.

296
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,200
Don't bother. I'll do it myself.

297
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,200
I'll do it myself.

298
00:15:47,150 --> 00:15:49,010
Have some water. Have some water.

299
00:15:55,030 --> 00:15:55,560
Benshan.

300
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,650
I think the information you just reported

301
00:15:58,720 --> 00:15:59,910
is very good

302
00:16:00,670 --> 00:16:01,730
and very valuable.

303
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,150
But

304
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,880
why didn't you report it

305
00:16:05,910 --> 00:16:07,840
to the organization immediately?

306
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:12,540
Actually, I did report it.

307
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:14,880
I reported it to Director Hong.

308
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,920
You even dare to hang up on me now?

309
00:16:17,350 --> 00:16:19,000
If I hadn't taken you in back then,

310
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,480
you would have gone back home
to build reservoirs long ago.

311
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,210
Liang Aimin,

312
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:23,730
watch your tone!

313
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,190
I'm a regimental‑level officer,

314
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:27,320
with over 20 years of Party membership,

315
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,650
2 second-class merits,

316
00:16:28,750 --> 00:16:30,210
and 3 third-class merits.

317
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:31,360
I can shine and contribute

318
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,080
anywhere I go.

319
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,240
And you took me in?

320
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,080
I'm doing this for the sake of our years

321
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,270
as comrades-in-arms.

322
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:38,000
I'm helping you. Don't you get that?

323
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:38,400
Right.

324
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:39,040
Thank you.

325
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:40,870
And do you know how many times

326
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:42,330
I've cleaned up your mess?

327
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,520
He supports Li Xiang.

328
00:16:45,410 --> 00:16:46,770
Director Hong

329
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,920
isn't very competent professionally,

330
00:16:50,290 --> 00:16:52,350
and his style of work is rather rough.

331
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:53,800
I've heard about it.

332
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,480
Besides,

333
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,600
I couldn't bypass my superiors

334
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,660
to report this sort of matter, right?

335
00:16:57,770 --> 00:16:58,440
No matter what,

336
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,220
our Justice Bureau

337
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,480
is still a state‑run institution, right?

338
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,270
What are you afraid of?

339
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,330
What am I afraid of?

340
00:17:02,490 --> 00:17:03,720
Secretary Su called out

341
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,319
your Legal Advisory Office.

342
00:17:07,089 --> 00:17:08,970
I only cursed at you once or twice.

343
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:09,920
I didn't curse at any leader.

344
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,119
Why did he call me out?

345
00:17:15,510 --> 00:17:16,829
Pleading not guilty is legal, isn't it?

346
00:17:16,829 --> 00:17:17,240
Right.

347
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:18,990
Isn't a lawyer's diligent defense

348
00:17:18,990 --> 00:17:20,579
a mission and a right

349
00:17:21,109 --> 00:17:22,240
granted to us by law?

350
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:23,460
Cut the grand talk.

351
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,550
Even if you can't keep up
with the current trend,

352
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:27,280
you can't go against it, right?

353
00:17:27,829 --> 00:17:29,550
Right now, national incidence rate
of criminal cases

354
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:30,750
is dropping rapidly.

355
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:33,110
Public order
has significantly improved.

356
00:17:33,110 --> 00:17:35,550
People's sense of safety
has been enhanced.

357
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:36,720
At this critical moment,

358
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,410
you argue that a person
sentenced to death is innocent,

359
00:17:38,410 --> 00:17:39,110
and that rape resulting in death

360
00:17:39,110 --> 00:17:40,640
is just a matter of personal conduct.

361
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:41,510
Do you have any idea

362
00:17:41,510 --> 00:17:43,170
how big a bomb you've dropped?

363
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:46,830
So before the organization came to you,

364
00:17:46,830 --> 00:17:47,690
what did you do?

365
00:17:48,830 --> 00:17:50,690
I firmly fought against Li Xiang,

366
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,000
but...

367
00:17:52,110 --> 00:17:52,680
But

368
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,550
you weren't firm enough, right?

369
00:17:54,550 --> 00:17:55,180
Secretary Sun.

370
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:55,860
I... I...

371
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,840
I'm really no match for them.

372
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,480
They've got their little groups

373
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,920
and small factions in the Advisory Office,

374
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:02,550
so I...

375
00:18:02,830 --> 00:18:04,550
So you just played it safe?

376
00:18:08,350 --> 00:18:09,480
It's okay, Benshan.

377
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,640
We know where you stand.

378
00:18:12,670 --> 00:18:13,440
Otherwise, we wouldn't be

379
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,300
having this conversation today.

380
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:16,130
Do you understand?

381
00:18:16,130 --> 00:18:17,190
Yes, I understand.

382
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:20,190
It's about fixing mistakes
before it's too late.

383
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:21,970
It's fine. Don't worry.

384
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:23,400
Report what you know

385
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,110
to the organization,

386
00:18:24,110 --> 00:18:25,080
truthfully

387
00:18:25,110 --> 00:18:26,640
and in as much detail as possible.

388
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,160
Because you're the primary witness.

389
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,160
Every word you say

390
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,270
is very valuable.

391
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:32,270
Okay.

392
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:33,030
Okay.

393
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:36,530
Is it really that serious?

394
00:18:37,130 --> 00:18:37,990
Let me tell you,

395
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:39,840
don't be ungrateful.

396
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:42,070
Hurry up and write a self-criticism.

397
00:18:42,070 --> 00:18:42,510
Don't wait

398
00:18:42,510 --> 00:18:44,710
until even I can't protect you anymore.

399
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,850
Then I'll just quit.

400
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,750
You think quitting will solve everything?

401
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:54,350
Then what?

402
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:56,210
Are they going to arrest me?

403
00:18:56,550 --> 00:18:57,680
Has it really gotten to the point

404
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,920
where we have to make arrests?

405
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,550
The order has come down,
Court Pres. Ding.

406
00:19:00,550 --> 00:19:02,350
We must act according to the law,

407
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,820
earning the trust of the general public.

408
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:07,160
Li Xiang

409
00:19:08,110 --> 00:19:08,840
is too young,

410
00:19:09,310 --> 00:19:09,910
immature,

411
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:10,930
impulsive,

412
00:19:11,830 --> 00:19:13,450
and a bit tactless.

413
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,660
He deserves to be criticized.

414
00:19:16,230 --> 00:19:18,360
I agree that he should write a thorough

415
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:19,790
self-criticism.

416
00:19:21,090 --> 00:19:22,850
But there's no law stating

417
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:23,760
that a lawyer

418
00:19:24,270 --> 00:19:25,960
can't disagree

419
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,290
with the procuratorate

420
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:30,270
or can't plead not guilty, right?

421
00:19:32,510 --> 00:19:34,040
There isn't any legal basis

422
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:37,040
for arresting him, is there?

423
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:39,400
He openly defied the organization.

424
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,280
He covered up for the criminal.

425
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:42,790
He leaked state secrets to the criminal.

426
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:44,310
Isn't that a violation of the law?

427
00:19:44,310 --> 00:19:45,760
Leaked state secrets?

428
00:19:45,790 --> 00:19:46,160
Yes.

429
00:19:48,070 --> 00:19:49,000
What state secrets

430
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:49,920
did he leak?

431
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:01,550
You scared me.

432
00:20:01,550 --> 00:20:02,070
Let me help you.

433
00:20:02,070 --> 00:20:02,670
Thank you.

434
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:04,930
How come you walk like a cat?

435
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:05,750
No sound at all.

436
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:06,880
I used to be a scout.

437
00:20:08,020 --> 00:20:09,030
Who are you looking for?

438
00:20:09,030 --> 00:20:09,480
You.

439
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:10,270
Me?

440
00:20:10,970 --> 00:20:12,200
I've finished reading

441
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:13,530
those books you gave me.

442
00:20:13,770 --> 00:20:14,830
I don't have any new ones.

443
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:16,630
I only brought those textbooks.

444
00:20:17,310 --> 00:20:18,640
I wrote down my thoughts

445
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,250
and did some case analyses.

446
00:20:21,550 --> 00:20:22,810
If you have time,

447
00:20:23,030 --> 00:20:24,760
could you look them over for me?

448
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:35,200
I'm being a bit inconsiderate

449
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:37,190
and asking for too much.

450
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:38,830
Lihui.

451
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,900
Hurry. We're waiting for you.

452
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:46,420
Jian... Jianmin, why are you here?

453
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:46,740
Give them to me.

454
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:47,130
I...

455
00:20:47,150 --> 00:20:47,630
Zheng!

456
00:20:48,710 --> 00:20:49,510
Zheng! Zheng!

457
00:20:49,590 --> 00:20:51,110
Don't leave yet.

458
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:51,790
How about this?

459
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:53,570
Help Lihui carry the water upstairs.

460
00:20:53,570 --> 00:20:54,770
We want to talk to you.

461
00:20:58,030 --> 00:20:58,960
Come on. Come on.

462
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:01,210
Okay.

463
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:04,790
Thanks.

464
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,160
Don't mention it.

465
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,270
Go in.

466
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,480
Have a seat.

467
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:20,960
What's this about?

468
00:21:21,830 --> 00:21:22,230
Zheng,

469
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:24,420
you really don't know?

470
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:25,790
Know what?

471
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:29,640
This matter

472
00:21:30,510 --> 00:21:31,770
might be a bit serious.

473
00:21:32,510 --> 00:21:33,680
Don't scare him.

474
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:34,680
What's wrong?

475
00:21:37,590 --> 00:21:38,160
Jianmin,

476
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:40,420
we're only telling you this

477
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:41,620
because we trust you.

478
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:44,350
What is it?

479
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:47,590
Has Court Pres. Ding said anything to you

480
00:21:47,590 --> 00:21:49,050
about arresting Li Xiang?

481
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:51,240
Why?

482
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:52,350
Why?

483
00:21:54,330 --> 00:21:55,460
That's impossible.

484
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:58,170
Jianmin,

485
00:21:59,240 --> 00:21:59,980
has Court Pres. Ding

486
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:01,130
given you any hints

487
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:01,920
or...

488
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:03,400
No.

489
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:09,860
Even if he really intended
to make an arrest,

490
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:11,010
he wouldn't tell me.

491
00:22:13,310 --> 00:22:14,070
Arrests

492
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:15,510
should be the police's job.

493
00:22:15,510 --> 00:22:17,310
Why would they need Court Pres. Ding
for that?

494
00:22:17,310 --> 00:22:18,400
So we

495
00:22:19,270 --> 00:22:21,470
want you to do some digging internally.

496
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:22,830
Over the next few days,
try to get some information

497
00:22:22,830 --> 00:22:24,090
out of Court Pres. Ding

498
00:22:24,110 --> 00:22:25,240
and see if it's true.

499
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:26,440
If it is true,

500
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,110
we need to prepare in advance.

501
00:22:28,110 --> 00:22:30,510
It will be too late
once things get rolling.

502
00:22:31,110 --> 00:22:31,640
Jianmin,

503
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,280
we've always had

504
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:33,920
a good relationship.

505
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,790
I've always considered you a friend.

506
00:22:35,790 --> 00:22:37,920
Besides, Li Xiang really is a good guy.

507
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:38,960
He shouldn't become

508
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,220
a martyr for this case.

509
00:22:44,050 --> 00:22:44,940
You want me...

510
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:45,960
To put it bluntly,

511
00:22:46,150 --> 00:22:47,200
we want you

512
00:22:47,230 --> 00:22:48,230
to be a spy for us.

513
00:22:48,510 --> 00:22:49,910
That doesn't sound good.

514
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:50,790
It should be

515
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:52,350
a sharp knife

516
00:22:52,350 --> 00:22:54,080
thrust into the enemy's heart.

517
00:22:54,350 --> 00:22:56,410
But Court Pres. Ding isn't the enemy.

518
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:57,490
Isn't he?

519
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:07,520
What's so funny?

520
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:10,680
Fine.

521
00:23:11,550 --> 00:23:12,830
Even if I find out

522
00:23:13,790 --> 00:23:16,050
that they are indeed going to arrest him,

523
00:23:16,110 --> 00:23:17,310
what do you plan to do?

524
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:20,910
Chen Yizhong.

525
00:23:23,690 --> 00:23:25,620
Are you going to tell him in advance

526
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:27,140
so that he can abscond?

527
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:29,240
Talk him into resisting arrest?

528
00:23:29,510 --> 00:23:31,350
Or be his defense lawyer?

529
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:33,440
Or

530
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,370
stage protests?

531
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,330
File petitions?

532
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:38,370
Storm the judicial authorities?

533
00:23:38,370 --> 00:23:39,550
Or throw rotten eggs

534
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:40,840
and tomatoes at him

535
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:42,110
during the trial?

536
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:42,310
Come on,

537
00:23:42,310 --> 00:23:43,770
how could you be like this?

538
00:23:44,830 --> 00:23:45,680
Like what?

539
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:51,800
You want me to be your spy.

540
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:55,000
I work for the court.

541
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:58,930
I should just throw my job away?

542
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,000
And you don't want

543
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,860
your internship reports either?

544
00:24:05,030 --> 00:24:05,940
In a few months,

545
00:24:06,270 --> 00:24:07,730
you'll go back to Beijing.

546
00:24:07,830 --> 00:24:10,290
Will you take me, this sharp knife,
with you?

547
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,160
Or just leave me

548
00:24:11,160 --> 00:24:12,710
in the enemy's heart?

549
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:14,730
No, Jianmin.

550
00:24:15,790 --> 00:24:16,350
We're not doing this

551
00:24:16,350 --> 00:24:17,310
for ourselves.

552
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:18,660
We want to help Li Xiang.

553
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,030
For the progress of China's legal system,

554
00:24:20,030 --> 00:24:21,160
we want to do some...

555
00:24:25,550 --> 00:24:26,750
This proposition...

556
00:24:34,270 --> 00:24:34,920
I know

557
00:24:37,350 --> 00:24:38,550
you guys are very kind

558
00:24:41,310 --> 00:24:42,240
and passionate.

559
00:24:42,830 --> 00:24:45,030
You also have a strong sense of justice.

560
00:24:45,030 --> 00:24:48,160
But it's inappropriate
to make groundless accusations

561
00:24:48,590 --> 00:24:49,990
about this kind of thing.

562
00:25:00,550 --> 00:25:01,610
I won't tell anyone

563
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,750
what was said in this room today.

564
00:25:03,750 --> 00:25:04,110
Wait.

565
00:25:04,510 --> 00:25:05,310
Jianmin, could you...

566
00:25:05,310 --> 00:25:05,710
Lihui.

567
00:25:06,830 --> 00:25:07,680
Next time you need water,

568
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:08,880
let the guys carry it.

569
00:25:32,070 --> 00:25:32,930
Zheng Jianmin.

570
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:37,070
I'm sorry.

571
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,600
You don't need to apologize.

572
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:42,160
I'm quite regretful.

573
00:25:42,830 --> 00:25:44,230
I was a bit harsh just now.

574
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:45,680
It's nothing.

575
00:25:46,370 --> 00:25:47,290
I think we needed

576
00:25:47,290 --> 00:25:49,240
that reality check from your words.

577
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:50,240
It's a good thing.

578
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:51,880
I'm sorry.

579
00:25:53,750 --> 00:25:55,280
Zhang Lihui, you know what?

580
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:56,740
Out of the five of you,

581
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:58,540
I think you stand out the most.

582
00:25:59,350 --> 00:26:01,110
If you said
I'm the easiest to get along with,

583
00:26:01,110 --> 00:26:02,110
I'd believe that.

584
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:03,360
Stand out the most...

585
